{"name":"Peekaboo","hex":"#e6dee6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"peekaboo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A game for a small child in which one covers one's face, then suddenly reveals it, saying \"Boo!\" or \"Peekaboo!\"."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["With holes, slits or transparent fabric to reveal what is normally hidden.","Being or using a style of boxing with the hands kept close to the face to defend it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peekaboo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Peekaboo","blocks":[{"text":"Peekaboo is a simple game played with an infant. To play, one player hides their face, pops back into the view of the other, and says Peekaboo!, sometimes followed by I see you! There are many variations: for example, where trees are involved, \"Hiding behind that tree!\" is sometimes added. Another variation involves saying \"Where's the baby?\" while the face is covered and \"There's the baby!\" when uncovering the face."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Inai-inai-baa_peak-a-boo_8jo_WATANABEhachijo.gif/330px-Inai-inai-baa_peak-a-boo_8jo_WATANABEhachijo.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peekaboo","wikidata":"Q53705"},{"title":"Peekaboo (musician)","blocks":[{"text":"Matthew Austin Lucas, better known by his alias Peekaboo, is an American dubstep producer. Although he began as a multi-genre electronic music artist, he is mostly now known for his particular style of dubstep, also known as freeform bass and space bass. His sixth extended play Wrecking Ball debuted at #10 on Billboard's Dance/Electronic Album Sales chart in early 2019."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peekaboo_(musician)","wikidata":"Q61819897"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Kou-Kou_by_Georgios_Iakovidis.jpg/500px-Kou-Kou_by_Georgios_Iakovidis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Kou-Kou_by_Georgios_Iakovidis.jpg/500px-Kou-Kou_by_Georgios_Iakovidis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Two children playing peekaboo (1895 painting by Georgios Jakobides)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKou-Kou_by_Georgios_Iakovidis.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/US_Navy_100406-N-7478G-346_Operations_Specialist_2nd_Class_Reginald_Harlmon_and_Electronics_Technician_3rd_Class_Maura_Schulze_play_peek-a-boo_with_a_child_in_the_Children%27s_Ward_at_Hospital_Likas.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/US_Navy_100406-N-7478G-346_Operations_Specialist_2nd_Class_Reginald_Harlmon_and_Electronics_Technician_3rd_Class_Maura_Schulze_play_peek-a-boo_with_a_child_in_the_Children%27s_Ward_at_Hospital_Likas.jpg/1280px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/US_Navy_100406-N-7478G-346_Operations_Specialist_2nd_Class_Reginald_Harlmon_and_Electronics_Technician_3rd_Class_Maura_Schulze_play_peek-a-boo_with_a_child_in_the_Children%27s_Ward_at_Hospital_Likas.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Peekaboo is a prime example of an object permanence test in childhood cognition.[4]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUS_Navy_100406-N-7478G-346_Operations_Specialist_2nd_Class_Reginald_Harlmon_and_Electronics_Technician_3rd_Class_Maura_Schulze_play_peek-a-boo_with_a_child_in_the_Children's_Ward_at_Hospital_Likas.jpg"}],"sounds":{"peekaboo":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/63/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-peekaboo.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/63/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-peekaboo.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-peekaboo.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/63/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-peekaboo.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-peekaboo.wav.ogg"}]}}}